            <ArticleTitle>Art therapy for schizophrenia?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e6845</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5867/medwave.2017.6845</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Art therapy is used as a complementary treatment to antipsychotics in schizophrenia. However, its effectiveness is not clear. To answer this question, we searched in Epistemonikos database, which is maintained by screening multiple databases. We identified five systematic reviews including 20 studies overall, of which four were randomized trials. We extracted data and prepared summary of findings tables using the GRADE method. We concluded it is not clear whether art therapy leads to clinical improvement in schizophrenia because the certainty of the evidence is very low.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
